remstart
    THE SQUID
    another hidden thing of the night. nothing in the game says that it is there, and the only way to see
    it is its picture. the routines are in fish_routines_squid, and the tests are in fish_tests_squid.
    see THE TIDE in fish_headers_tide for the night.

    IT COMES AT NIGHTFALL. once night has fallen and the board has settled, one fish that has no fish of
    its own kind next to it turns into a squid. it is picked with the board's own stream of numbers, so a
    seed gets the same squid. a fish next to one of its kind is never picked, so the squid never spoils a
    group that is nearly made. the fish is still there, under the squid: CELLS().value keeps its kind,
    and SQUID_CELL says which cell the squid is in. while it is there, the cell is the squid, and not the
    fish: it is drawn as the squid, and it never matches anything. findCombos leaves it out.

    A PUSH. a swap that has the squid on either end of it is not a swap. it is the squid being pushed,
    the way that the swap would have moved it: carried, when the cursor is on the squid, and shoved
    back, when the cursor comes at it from next door. it can be pushed off of the edge of the board.
    nothing trades places. the squid puffs away into a cloud of its ink, the cell that it was in is
    inked, the fish that was under it grows back in, and the squid escapes along the row or the column that it was pushed down, and takes over the fish
    of the cell that it gets to, whatever is there, growing in there. the cursor stays where it was. it is one of the
    moves of the night, the same as a swap. startLiveMove, in fish_funcs, sends a push to squidPushed.

    WHERE IT GOES. it goes the way that it was pushed, and around the edge of the board and back in on
    the other side. how far is the number of kinds before a repeat: walking on from the squid, the kinds
    of the cells that it passes are counted, starting with the fish right next to it, and the walk stops
    at the first kind that has been seen already. the squid goes as many cells as there were kinds, and
    lands on the last new one. so on a row that goes (the squid), A, B, C, A, it goes 3, and lands on the
    C. the fish under the squid does not count, because it cannot be seen. it goes at least one, and when
    a whole lap has no repeat, it stops one short of where it started. squidJump works it out. nothing on
    the screen says any of this.

    THE INK. a cell is inked, or it is not. ink is the cell's, and not the fish's: it stays where it is.
    it only goes where it is dragged, by day as well as by night: a swap that starts on an inked cell inks
    the cell that the cursor goes to, and the ink comes along with the cursor, a stroke out of the cell
    that it was in. a swap that goes into ink from outside of it does nothing to the ink.
    so a stroke can be drawn out from any ink that there is, a cell at a time. only a push of the squid
    starts ink anywhere new, so ink that is in more than one piece is a sign of a squid that was pushed
    on purpose. the ink is moved as the swap starts, and flows along with the cursor. inkSwapStarted does it.
    CORAL WINS. at night, ink goes onto coral like anywhere else. by day, coral will not have it: ink that
    is moved onto coral lurches toward it, and breaks up into little bubbles, and the coral is not inked.
    ink that is on coral when day breaks, which is not the day's, and ink that coral grows onto, breaks
    up the same way. inkCoralWins does that, whenever the coral has changed.
    THE END OF THE NIGHT. when the last move of the night is made and there is ink, the night holds on
    until the board has settled, since the last move may have made a constellation, and then until the
    constellation has popped. then day breaks. a move that is made while it waits is not counted at all. squidNightEnds and squidStep do this. the squid goes when day breaks.

    THE INK OF THE DAY. the ink that is left when day breaks stays, and dries: it is dark and nearly
    solid, with a lighter edge around the whole of it. a fish that pops on an inked cell washes the ink
    off of it (inkWashed, from handle_combos), and swaps still move it.
    CLEAN. a cell that has been washed is clean, and it shows: a glow behind its fish, and a pale edge
    around the clean cells, the other way around from the ink. it stays clean if ink is moved back onto
    it, and is washed again: a cell is only ever clean once. INK_CLEAN has them.
    THE POT is how many clean cells there are. when the last of the ink is washed off, the pot pays: a
    the clean cells poof away in a sparkle, one after another at a steady pace, the nearest to the one
    that was washed last first, with a glow running on ahead of them like a wave, each with a pop that
    is higher than the last, and its score. each is worth INK_POT_STEP more than the one before it, so a pot of n pays
    INK_POT_STEP * n * (n + 1) / 2, times the multiplier. so to make the pot bigger, the ink has to be
    moved onto cells that have not been washed yet, and washed off of them: washing the same cell over
    and over is worth nothing.
    a pot that is not washed off by nightfall is lost: the ink breaks up, the clean cells fade, and it
    is worth INK_BUST_POINTS a clean cell. the night's ink starts from nothing. inkPotStep and inkBust do this.
    ink that goes, however it goes, goops up into bubbles that break away: see THE FIZZ.

    the ink is drawn by InkEffect.fx, on one sprite over the whole board, under the fish. at night it is
    dark and soft, with a light that runs along its edge, and a glow that spills out into the water. ink
    in cells that touch at a side is one smear, with no seam. the cell that was inked last spreads out
    from nothing, or flows into it along with the cursor. by day it is the dried ink: the same wobbling
    blots, swollen, so that ink in cells that touch is one solid smear, and four that meet have no hole
    between them, dark, with a lighter edge, and a faint, shimmering reflection of the fish over it. all
    of it, by night and by day, has a slow cloud of dark blues and purples through it, which is fixed to
    the screen, and not to the ink. the reflection is the
    picture of each fish, which the coral's shadows draw to a render target of their own: see THE FISH
    CAST SHADOWS in fish_headers. it goes from the one look to the other as day breaks. the clean cells are
    drawn on the same sprite.

    THE CONSTELLATIONS. as night falls, up to three shapes come out in the open water either side of the
    board, made of the plankton, the little lights that drift up through the water at night: an easy one,
    a middling one and a hard one. they ARE the plankton, so they rise and sway with it. HintSnowEffect.fx
    lights the grains of the shape's stars, on a little grid, and SeabedEffect.fx leaves its own lights out
    of the box of the shape. there is one in the water at a time: it fades in low beside the board, rises
    with the plankton, and every so often lines sweep across it, joining up the lights of each piece, hold,
    and fade, and it is plankton again. near the top it fades out, and as it does, the next shape fades in
    low on the other side of the board. the shapes take turns. a player who does not know to look sees plankton. a player who is looking
    sees a few lights in a neat little grid, and every so often the lines say what the shape is. see THE HINTS IN THE SNOW, and starSkyDraw. the easy ones and the middling
    ones are one piece, and the hard one two. drawing one in ink, exactly, in any of its four turns, makes it. exactly means
    that every piece of it is a piece of ink of its own: inked, and with no other ink touching it at a
    side. ink that touches it only at a corner is not touching it. ink anywhere else is fine.
    the shapes are the parts of the trident of the god. see THE TRIDENT in fish_headers_neptune, which
    has which part is which, and ONE A NIGHT: once one is made, the others fade for the rest of the night.
    the easy ones are 6 cells, the middling ones 7 and the hard one 9, and the night has 12 moves, and no
    move inks more than one cell, so the hard one leaves the least room. a shape that is not needed any
    more does not come out. THE EASY ONES FIRST: only the easiest kind that the game still needs is
    hinted at in the water, the easy ones until both are made, then the middling ones, and the shaft
    last. see starSkyDraw. EVERY ONE CAN BE MADE: any shape that the game does not have yet can be made on
    any night, hinted at or not, so a player who remembers one can make it. starLook tries the shape of
    the night of each kind first, then the others of that kind. an easy or middling one is
    one piece: a push starts it, and swaps out of the ink grow it, so where the squid happens to jump
    does not keep a player from it. the hard one is two pieces, neither of them a single cell, which line
    up along a row or a column, so that a player who knows where the squid goes can get it from one to
    the other. build/star_odds.py says how
    often each can be made on a board as it is dealt.
    once a constellation is made, it is kept, whatever the ink does after. its cells are the
    constellation's, and no other constellation can be made of them. both the ink and its hint in the
    water shimmer, and a fanfare plays. then, STAR_POP_WAIT later, it pops: every fish of it scores
    STAR_BONUS times what it would as a fish of a group that size, and its ink goes. starPop does it.

    the "Tide" window of the debug panel (FISH_DEBUG) puts the squid on the cursor, says where it would go
    for every push, inks the cursor's cell, wipes the ink, keeps the night from ending, and says which
    constellations are made.
remend

global TEX_SQUID `its picture. setup_squid loads it. it is not a kind of fish: the cell keeps the kind of the fish under it.
global SQUID_CELL = -1 `the cell that the squid is in, or -1 when there is none
global SQUID_DUE = 0 `1 when night has fallen, and the squid comes as soon as the board has settled
global SQUID_SHOWN_CELL = -1 `the cell that is drawn as the squid, so that the fish can be put back when it goes
global SQUID_FREE_PUSH = 0 `1 while startFreeMove is starting its swap, so that a push of the "free move" card is not counted
global SQUID_PUSHES = 0 `how many times the squid has been pushed tonight
global dim SQUID_SEEN(64) `scratch, for squidJump: the stamp of the walk that saw every kind
global SQUID_SEEN_STAMP = 0
global SQUID_ENDLESS = 0 `1 to keep the night from ending, from the debug panel
global SQUID_ENDING = 0 `THE END OF THE NIGHT: 1 when the night is over, and day breaks once the board has settled and the constellation has popped

` THE PUFF. the squid that is pushed puffs away into its ink, and the fish under it grows back in.
global SQUID_GHOST = 0 `the sprite of the squid that puffs away, made the first time that it is needed
global SQUID_PUFF_CELL = -1
global SQUID_PUFF_MS = 0 `when it started, or 0 when it is over
global SQUID_PUFF_LONG# = 420 `how long it takes, in milliseconds
global SQUID_BACK_CELL = -1 `the cell whose fish is growing back in
global SQUID_BACK_MS = 0 `when it starts to
global SQUID_BACK_DELAY = 120 `how long after the push that is
global SQUID_IN_CELL = -1 `the cell that the squid is growing in, where it landed
global SQUID_IN_MS = 0
global SQUID_IN_DELAY = 230
global SQUID_GROW_LONG# = 380 `how long growing in takes

` THE INK
global dim INK(400) `1 for every cell that is inked
global INK_COUNT = 0
global INK_FX_ID = 0
global INK_BOARD_SPRITE = 0 `the one sprite that all of the ink is drawn on, over the board. made the first time that it is needed.
global INK_GONE_MS = 0 `when the ink popped, so that it fades out, or 0
global INK_FADE_MS# = 700 `how long it takes to fade out
global INK_FRESH_CELL = -1 `the cell that was inked last, whose ink spreads out from nothing
global INK_FRESH_MS = 0 `and when
global INK_FRESH_FROM = -1 `the inked cell that it spread from, which it flows out of, or -1 when it came from nothing
global INK_SPREAD_MS = 600 `how long new ink that comes from nothing takes to spread out to the size of its cell
global INK_FRESH_LONG = 600 `how long the fresh ink takes to get there: INK_SPREAD_MS, or as long as the cursor takes, when it flows along with it
global INK_LAND_LONG = 280 `and how long it wobbles for, once it has landed
global ORDER_INK = 7 `on top of the sea floor and the coral, and underneath the cursor and the fish
global INK_DIRTY = 0 `1 when the ink has changed, and the constellations have to be looked for again
global INK_BOARD_COLS = 0 `how many columns the board had on the last frame. when it grows, the night's ink is wiped.
global INK_ROWS_STALE = 1 `1 when the bits below have to be worked out again
global dim INK_ROW_BITS(20) `a number for every row, with a bit for every inked cell of it. InkEffect.fx takes them.
global dim MADE_ROW_BITS(20) `and the same for the cells of made constellations
global dim INK_ROW#(20) `the same numbers, as floats, the way that the effect takes them
global dim MADE_ROW#(20)
global dim INK_POW(20) `two to the power of every column. setup_squid fills it in.
global dim INK_WASH_MS(400) `when the ink of a cell that was washed off goes from the screen, which is when its fish pops, or 0
global INK_WASH_NEXT = 0 `the soonest of those that is still to come, or 0
global INK_SHOWN_COUNT = 0 `how many cells are drawn inked, which is how many pips of the pot are lit
global INK_CORAL_SEEN = -1 `how much coral there was when the ink was last looked at for it. see CORAL WINS.
global INK_INK_RGB = 0 `the color of a puff of the ink. setup_squid sets it.

` CORAL WINS. ink that is moved onto coral by day lurches toward it, and breaks up into bubbles at the tip.
global INK_LURCH_FROM = -1 `the inked cell that it lurches out of, or -1
global INK_LURCH_TO = -1 `the coral that it lurches toward
global INK_LURCH_MS = 0 `when it started
global INK_LURCH_LONG = 160 `how long it reaches for, which is as long as the cursor takes
global INK_LURCH_BACK = 240 `and how long what is left of it takes to shrink back
global INK_LURCH_BROKE = 0 `1 once its tip has broken up
global INK_LURCH_REACH# = 0.62 `how far it gets, in cells

` THE INK OF THE DAY, AND THE POT
global INK_DAY = 0 `1 while the ink on the board is the day's, and the pot is on it
global INK_DAY_SHOWN# = 0 `how much the ink is drawn the day's way, from 0 to 1. it chases INK_DAY.
global INK_DAY_EASE# = 0.003 `how much of the way it goes in a millisecond
global INK_DRAW_LAST_MS = 0 `when the ink was last drawn
global INK_POT = 0 `how many clean cells there are, which is what the pot is. see THE POT.
global dim INK_CLEAN(400) `1 for every cell that has been washed since day broke. see CLEAN.
global INK_CLEAN_SHOWN = 0 `how many clean cells are drawn
global dim INK_CLEAN_BITS(20) `the clean cells that are drawn, a number for every row, the way that INK_ROW_BITS is
global dim INK_CLEAN_ROW#(20)
global INK_LAST_WASHED = -1 `the cell that was washed last, which the wave of the pot starts from
global INK_POT_STEP = 10 `how much more each clean cell of the pot is worth than the one before it, before the multiplier
global INK_BUST_POINTS = 2 `what each clean cell of a pot that is lost at nightfall is worth, before the multiplier
global INK_LAST_PAY = 0 `what the last pot paid, for the tests
global INK_LAST_BUST = 0 `and what the last lost one did
global INK_REFLECT = 0 `1 while the fish of the inked cells are drawn for their reflections. fish_routines_coral draws them.
global INK_ART_HALF# = 8 `half of how big a fish is drawn, where its reflection starts

` THE POT PAYS. the clean cells poof away one after another, the nearest to the one that was washed
` last first, at a steady pace, so that a bigger pot takes longer, each in its own sparkle, with its
` score. a glow runs on ahead of the next ones to go, like a wave. InkEffect.fx draws the glow, and
` InkFizzEffect.fx the poofs. the times are in milliseconds.
global INK_PAYING = 0 `1 while it pays
global INK_PAY_MS = 0 `when it started
global INK_PAY_COUNT = 0 `how many clean cells there are to poof
global INK_PAY_POINTS = 0 `and what they are worth all together
global dim INK_PAY_CELL(400) `the cells, nearest to where the wave starts first
global dim INK_PAY_AT(400) `and when each poofs, from when it started
global dim INK_PAY_FAR#(400) `and how far each is from where it starts, in cells, for the glow
global INK_PAY_POPPED = 0 `how many of them have poofed
global INK_PAY_FROM_X# = 0 `the cell that the wave starts from
global INK_PAY_FROM_Y# = 0
global INK_PAY_LEAD = 300 `how long after it starts the first one poofs, so that the swell is heard first
global INK_PAY_EVERY = 190 `how long after one poofs the next one does
global INK_PAY_POP_LONG = 650 `how long a cell takes to poof away
global INK_PAY_TEXT# = 1.3 `how big the words of each score are

` THE FIZZ. a cell whose ink goes, washed off, popped with its constellation, lost at nightfall, or
` broken up by coral, goops up into bubbles that break away and pop, with a fizz. a clean cell of the pot
` that pays poofs away the same way, in the look of a clean cell. every one is a sprite of its own, over the board's ink, with
` InkFizzEffect.fx on it, which is told how far along it is by the sprite's texcoord2. inkFizzStart and
` inkFizzStep do it.
#constant INK_FIZZ_GOO 0
#constant INK_FIZZ_POOF 1
global INK_FIZZ_MAX = 48
global dim INK_FIZZ_SPRITE(48)
global dim INK_FIZZ_ON(48) `1 while the sprite is in use
global dim INK_FIZZ_X(48) `where its middle is, in pixels
global dim INK_FIZZ_Y(48)
global dim INK_FIZZ_MS(48) `when it starts, on the clock of the game
global dim INK_FIZZ_MODE(48) `INK_FIZZ_GOO, or INK_FIZZ_POOF
global dim INK_FIZZ_SCALE#(48) `how big it is, from 0 to 1 of a cell's worth of ink
global dim INK_FIZZ_SEED(48)
global dim INK_FIZZ_SOUNDED(48) `1 once its sound has played
global INK_FIZZ_NEXT = 0 `the sprite to take when none is free
global INK_FIZZ_LIVE = 0 `how many are going
global INK_FIZZ_LONG = 900 `how long one takes
global INK_FIZZ_POOF_LONG = 650 `and a poof of the pot, which is INK_PAY_POP_LONG
global INK_FIZZ_SPAN# = 3 `how many cells across its sprite is, so that the bubbles have room to rise
global INK_FIZZ_FX = 0

` THE SOUNDS OF THE INK. each of the ones that can come close together has a few voices, which take turns.
global INK_SFX_SPREAD = 0 `a gloop, as ink flows into a cell
global dim INK_SFX_FIZZ(4) `ink breaking up into bubbles
global dim INK_SFX_POP(4) `a clean cell of the pot poofing away
global INK_SFX_FIZZ_NEXT = 0
global INK_SFX_POP_NEXT = 0
global INK_FIZZ_SOUND_MS = 0 `when a fizz last played, so that a group of them is not a wall of noise
global INK_VOL_SPREAD# = 0.5
global INK_VOL_FIZZ# = 0.4
global INK_VOL_POP# = 0.55

` THE POT IS LOST. the clean cells fade.
global INK_CRUMBLE_MS = 0 `when it was lost, or 0
global INK_CRUMBLE_LONG = 700

` the pieces of the ink. inkFindPieces works them out.
global dim INK_PIECE(400) `the piece that every inked cell is part of, from 1, or 0
global dim INK_PIECE_SIZE(400) `how many cells every piece has, by its number
global dim INK_STACK(400) `scratch, for the flood

` THE CONSTELLATIONS
#constant STAR_EASY 0
#constant STAR_MEDIUM 1
#constant STAR_HARD 2
global STAR_SHAPE_MAX = 16
global STAR_CELL_MAX = 160
global STAR_SHAPE_COUNT = 0
global dim STAR_SHAPE_TIER(16) `which of the three each shape is
